<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese bond report.</title>
<headline>Portuguese bond report.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese bonds were barely changed in quiet trade before the long Easter weekend and dealers expected little movement during the session.</p>
<p>The absence of Spanish financial markets and the Oporto derivatives market, which began their Easter breaks a day early, left cash bonds becalmed.</p>
<p>&quot;There will be no volatility and no liquidity today. Most of us have already gone on holiday,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>The escudo traded at 100.60/63 per mark after opening at 100.55/58.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
